{{also|hvad}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|hvat}}, originally the neuter form of {{m|non|*hver}} (from {{der|is|gem-pro|*hwaz}}), but conflated with {{m|non|hverr}} (whence Modern Icelandic {{m|is|hver}}). Corresponds to {{der|is|gem-pro|*hwat}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*kʷód}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kʷod}}. See {{m|is|hver}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/kʰvaːð/}} ({{audio|is|Is-hvað.oga|listen}})
* {{homophones|is|kvað}}
* {{IPA|is|/xʷaːð/}} {{q|dialectal, now rare}}
* {{rhymes|is|aːð|s=1}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun}}

# [[what]]
#: {{ux|is|'''Hvað''' gerði ég vitlaust?|'''What''' did I do wrong?}}
#: {{ux|is|Eftir '''hverju''' bíðum við?|'''What''' are we waiting for?}}

=====Declension=====
See {{m|is|hver}}.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|af hverju||why}}
* {{l|is|hvað segirðu||how are you}}

===Adverb===
{{head|is|adverb}}

# (with reference to an adjective or an adverb) [[how]]
#: {{ux|is|'''Hvað''' er dóttir þín gömul?|'''How''' old is your daughter?}}
#: {{ux|is|Þeir vissu ekki '''hvað''' þeir yrðu lengi í burtu.|They didn't know '''how''' long they would be away.}}